         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = 2 x^{3} + 2 \\). Then \\( du = 6 x^{2}\\,dx \\), so the integrand is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\) times \\( e^{u} \\) du: \\( \\frac{3}{2}\\int e^{u}\\,du \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99002",
         "rule_named": "substitution"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The limits change with the variable: x = 0 gives u = 2 and x = 1 gives u = 4, so the integral is \\( \\frac{3}{2}\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{2}^{4} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "limits converted to u"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluating gives \\( - \\frac{3 e^{2}}{2} + \\frac{3 e^{4}}{2} \\).",
